# Cleopatra: closer to the pyramids or the Moon?
subtitle: "Place the Great Pyramid, Cleopatra and the Moon landing on one timeline, and see how 'ancient' Egypt stretches across time."

## Cleopatra: closer to the pyramids or the Moon?
affirm: playful
text: {"font_size":32}
sources:
    - id: pyr
      title: Great Pyramid of Giza
      authors: Encyclopaedia Britannica
      year: 2024
      finding: built for the pharaoh Khufu, finished around 2560 BC
    - id: cleo
      title: Cleopatra
      authors: Encyclopaedia Britannica
      year: 2024
      finding: born 69 BC, died 30 BC; a Ptolemy of Macedonian descent, said by Plutarch to be the first of her line to learn Egyptian

    card title "Closer to the pyramids, or the Moon?"

Did Cleopatra live closer in time to the builders of the Great Pyramid, or to the first Moon landing?
    scale time cites ["pyr","cleo"] x 100 y 420 width 800 min -3000 max 2000 ticks 5

Here are the three moments: the pyramid is finished, Cleopatra dies, and Apollo 11 lands.
    cards when size 1.15 look flat along time
        * "Great Pyramid" icon.of pyramid icon.or ["triangle"] value -2560
        * "Cleopatra dies" icon.of crown icon.set twemoji value -30
        * "Moon landing" icon.of rocket icon.set twemoji value 1969

    ask "When did each happen? Drag each card to its year on the timeline." on when store w tolerance 0.06
        right: All {w.total} close.
        wrong: {w.within} of {w.total} close.

The Great Pyramid was finished around 2560 BC, for the pharaoh Khufu.
    highlight when_1

That is about two and a half thousand years before Cleopatra died.
    arrow gap1 #b5482e from.x 170.4 from.y 300 to.x 575.2 to.y 300
    text gap1_l "2,530 years" #b5482e x 372.8 y 255 font_size 32

She died in 30 BC.
    highlight when_2

And from her death to the Moon landing in 1969 is less than two thousand years.
    arrow gap2 #2f6b8f from.x 575.2 from.y 300 to.x 895.04 to.y 300
    text gap2_l "< 2,000 years" #2f6b8f x 735.12 y 255 font_size 32

So Cleopatra lived closer to Neil Armstrong than to the pyramid builders.
    highlight gap2 gap2_l

To her, the pyramids were already ancient: older to her than she is to us.
    highlight when_1

And she was not Egyptian by descent. Her family, the Ptolemies, were Macedonian Greeks, and Plutarch says she was the first of them to learn Egyptian.
    highlight when_2
